          "text": "CH'ÊNG K'o-kung 成克鞏 (T. 子固, H. 青壇), 1608–1691, official and scholar, was a native of Ta-ming, Chihli, third son of Ch'êng Chi-ming 成基命 (T. 靖之, H. 毖予, posthumous name 文穆, d. 1635) a chin-shih of 1607 and Grand Secretary under the Ming dynasty.",
